   8:     Fill triangular green and blue wedges around a left-anchored red horizontal segment.
   9: 
  10:     Input structure:
  11:     - The grid has an empty background and exactly one foreground object.
  12:     - The foreground object is a red horizontal segment starting at the left edge.
  13: 
  14:     Rule:
  15:     - Preserve the red segment.
  16:     - Above the red segment, fill left-aligned rows green with width equal to the segment length plus distance above.
  17:     - Below the red segment, fill left-aligned rows blue with width equal to the segment length minus distance below.
  18: 
  19:     Key insight:
  20:     - The red segment is the shared base width; moving upward expands the fill by one cell per row, while moving downward shrinks it by one cell per row.
  21:     """
  22:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  23:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
  24:     height, width = map(int, g.shape)
  25: 
