  74: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  75:     """
  76:     Use a colored control matrix to recolor a matching lattice of gray 3x3 template masks.
  77: 
  78:     Input structure
  79:     - The background contains a rectangular lattice of same-color 3x3 template objects, spaced by one background row and column.
  80:     - The remaining foreground pixels form a dense rectangular control matrix whose height and width match the template lattice.
  81:     - Each template object may have holes, but all objects in the lattice share the same 3x3 bbox geometry.
  82: 
  83:     Rule
  84:     - Match each control-matrix pixel to the template object at the same row and column in the lattice.
  85:     - Recolor only that template object's foreground pixels to the matched control color.
  86:     - Leave background holes, the control matrix, and all other pixels unchanged.
  87: 
  88:     Key insight
  89:     The colored matrix is a legend indexed by lattice position; it does not draw new shapes, it recolors the existing template masks in place.
